  "source": "[\\set.property(X_)]\nDefines: phi(X_) is (? is \\set) -> (? is \\\\statement)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"set property\"\n. description: \"A set property is a predicate on sets: given a set it yields a\n                statement, true or false. Properties are what the specification\n                axiom uses to carve subsets out of existing sets.\"\nId: \"cc680a81-3338-4848-8b9d-fcf368dd759e\"",
